          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 9.5"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.126,
            0.513,
            0.141
          ],
          "content": "n **Take a convex mirror. Hold it in one hand.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.141,
            0.618,
            0.156
          ],
          "content": "n **Hold a pencil in the upright position in the other hand.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.156,
            0.698,
            0.184
          ],
          "content": "**Observe the image of the pencil in the mirror. Is the image erect or inverted? Is it diminished or enlarged?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.184,
            0.698,
            0.214
          ],
          "content": "**Move the pencil away from the mirror slowly. Does the image become smaller or larger?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.213,
            0.698,
            0.259
          ],
          "content": "**Repeat this Activity carefully. State whether the image will move closer to or farther away from the focus as the object is moved away from the mirror?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.099,
            0.276,
            0.724,
            0.374
          ],
          "content": "**We consider two positions of the object for studying the image formed by a convex mirror. First is when the object is at infinity and the second position is when the object is at a finite distance from the mirror. The ray diagrams for the formation of image by a convex mirror for these two positions of the object are shown in Fig.9.8 (a) and (b), respectively. The results are summarised in Table 9.2.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.384,
            0.911,
            0.536
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.311,
                0.541,
                0.716,
                0.556
              ],
              "content": "Figure 9.8 Formation of image by a convex mirror"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_7_image_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.102,
            0.59,
            0.922,
            0.726
          ],
          "content": "| Position of the | Position of the | Size of the | Nature of the |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| object | image | image | image |\n| At infinity | At the focus F, behind the mirror | Highly diminished, point-sized | Virtual and erect |\n| Between infinity | Between P and F, | Diminished | Virtual and erect |\n| and the pole P of | behind the mirror |  |  |\n| the mirror |  |  |  |",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.1,
                0.568,
                0.839,
                0.584
              ],
              "content": "Table 9.2 Nature, position and relative size of the image formed by a convex mirror"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_7_table_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.732,
            0.724,
            0.783
          ],
          "content": "**You have so far studied the image formation by a plane mirror, a concave mirror and a convex mirror. Which of these mirrors will give the full image of a large object? Let us explore through an Activity.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.143,
            0.793,
            0.298,
            0.815
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 9.6"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.828,
            0.699,
            0.857
          ],
          "content": "**Observe the image of a distant object, say a distant tree, in a plane mirror.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.857,
            0.446,
            0.873
          ],
          "content": "n **Could you see a full-length image?**"
        },
        {
